# Build artifacts
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeScripts/
CTestTestfile.cmake
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt
# Per-machine preset overrides — committed CMakePresets.json holds the
# project-level presets; CMakeUserPresets.json layers in each developer's
# local Qt / vcpkg / FFmpeg paths.
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Qt-specific
*.qmake.stash
*.qmake.cache
.qmlls.ini
.qmlls.build.ini

# Qt CMake build artifacts that escape to the source tree when someone
# configures CMake with `-B <src-subdir>` instead of the canonical
# build-release/. These are all regenerated on every build; tracking
# them is what caused the cafe11f4 disaster (committed an entire
# in-tree build dir with paths like src/app/.rcc/qmlcache/qcview_../...
# that Windows literally cannot check out — `qcview_..` is an illegal
# NTFS directory name). Patterns intentionally match at any depth so
# the safety holds regardless of where the accidental -B points.
**/.qt/
**/.rcc/
**/*_autogen/
**/meta_types/
**/qmltypes/
**/*_qmltyperegistrations.cpp
# qt_add_qml_module's per-module staging dir (target_path-derived).
# For the qcview target the URI is "Qcv", so its in-tree staging
# would be src/app/Qcv/ — generated, not the source QML location
# (those live in src/ui/qml/).
src/app/Qcv/
# CMake's Makefile generator output; the canonical setup is Ninja
# (see CMakePresets.json), so any in-tree Makefile is a misconfigured
# build pointing at the source tree.
src/**/Makefile

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.user.*
.qtcreator/
compile_commands.json

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.app/

# Editor backups
*~
*.swp
*.bak

# Environment / local config
.env
.env.local

# Test outputs / scratch
/tmp/
/scratch/
*.log
# Runtime artifacts that escape to repo root if the app is launched
# from here (qcview-stdout.log + qcview-stderr.log + the internal
# qcview-log.txt tee). Already covered by *.log but listed explicitly
# so it's obvious why they're ignored.
qcview-stderr.log
qcview-stdout.log
qcview-log.txt
qcview-log.prev.txt
# Generic scratch dir for one-off captures during debugging.
TEMP/

# Per-machine build / signing scripts. They reference local dev-cert
# subjects, Homebrew paths, vendored-deps layouts, etc. — not useful
# to share via git, and the signing ones contain the developer identity
# string (CN / Team ID) baked into the codesign default. Each build
# machine keeps its own copies in scripts/ locally. The release runbook
# (scripts/RELEASE.md) lives with them — it documents the local scripts +
# machine-specific paths/identity, so it's kept local too.
scripts/*.sh
scripts/*.md

# Vendored deps tree produced by scripts/build_macos_deps.sh —
# 70+ MB of FFmpeg / OCIO / OpenEXR / etc. built for deployment
# target. Source not in tree; the script rebuilds it on demand.
external/install/
external/source/
external/build/

# Vendored Windows FFmpeg (BtbN GPL-Shared 8.1 branch) — the default
# QCV_BTBN_FFMPEG_DIR. ~200 MB of prebuilt DLLs/libs (avcodec-62.dll
# alone is ~98 MB); main auto-pushes to GitHub which hard-blocks
# >=100 MB files, so these are never committed. Re-fetch per
# dependencies.md §2 / dependencies-changelog.md.
external/ffmpeg-win64/

# Local Claude Code / agent config
.claude/

# MSIX packaging — staged inputs and packed outputs
installer/msix/staging/
installer/msix/dist/

# Sideload signing assets — private dev cert (.pfx) and its public .cer.
# Kept locally; never committed. Each developer / build machine copies
# these in from secure storage. The build script reads QCV_SIGNING_PFX
# pointing at this directory.
installer/sideload/
external/Sparkle/
sparkle_private_key*.txt
